</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Tielsch</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Vijan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Saaddine</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The economic burden of major adult visual disorders in the United States</article-title><source>Archives of Ophthalmology</source><year>2006</year><volume>124</volume><fpage>1754</fpage><lpage>1760</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17159036</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Salm</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Belsky</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Sloan</surname><given-names>FA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Trends in cost of major eye diseases to Medicare, 1991 to 2000</article-title><source>Am J Ophthalmol</source><year>2006</year><volume>142</volume><fpage>976</fpage><lpage>982</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17157582</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gupta</surname><given-names>OP</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>GC</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Age-related macular degeneration: the costs to society and the patient</article-title><source>Curr Opin Ophthalmol</source><year>2007</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>201</fpage><lpage>205</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17435426</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schmier</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>Halpern</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Covert</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Delgado</surname><g